    "body": "Both Chromium 64 and Firefox 57 load the CSS with no value for `Content-Type` set\r\n\r\n```\r\n<?php \r\n\r\n    header(\"Content-Type: \");\r\n    echo \"body{color:blue}\";\r\n\r\nphp?>\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith `''` set as value of `Content-Type`\r\n\r\n```\r\n<?php \r\n\r\n    header(\"Content-Type: '' \");\r\n    echo \"body{color:blue}\";\r\n\r\nphp?>\r\n```\r\nChromium create an entry at `document.styleSheets` though the style rules are not applied. At Firefox the style rules are applied.",
