    "body": "@annevk Not entirely sure what the parameters of  a \"cross-origin\" stylesheet are? Do you mean where `Access-Control-Allow-Origin:*` header is not set?\r\n\r\nThese are the previous tests with suggested inclusions\r\n\r\n```\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html>\r\n\r\n<head>\r\n  <script>\r\n    function handleLinkLoadEvent(link) {\r\n      try {\r\n        console.log(`link load event for ${link.sheet.href}, cssText: ${link.sheet.cssRules[0].cssText}, computedStyle: ${window.getComputedStyle(document.querySelector(link.sheet.cssRules[0].selectorText)).color}`);\r\n      } catch (err) {\r\n        console.error(err, link.sheet.href);\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    function handleLinkErrorEvent(link) {\r\n      try {\r\n        console.log(`link error event for ${link.sheet.href}, cssText: ${link.sheet.cssRules[0].cssText}, computedStyle: ${window.getComputedStyle(document.querySelector(link.sheet.cssRules[0].selectorText)).color}`);\r\n      } catch (err) {\r\n        console.error(err, link.sheet.href);\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    onload = function() {\r\n      console.assert(document.styleSheets.length === document.querySelectorAll(\"p\").length, [document.styleSheets]);\r\n      console.log(document.styleSheets, document.styleSheets.length, document.querySelectorAll(\"p\").length);\r\n    }\r\n  </script>\r\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"style.css\" onload=\"handleLinkLoadEvent(this)\" onerror=\"handleLinkErrorEvent(this)\">\r\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"styleNoExtension\" onload=\"handleLinkLoadEvent(this)\" onerror=\"handleLinkErrorEvent(this)\">\r\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"data:,p:nth-child(3){color:green}\" onload=\"handleLinkLoadEvent(this)\" onerror=\"handleLinkErrorEvent(this)\">\r\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"data:unknown/unknown,p:nth-child(4){color:purple}\" onload=\"handleLinkLoadEvent(this)\" onerror=\"handleLinkErrorEvent(this)\">\r\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"data:application/unknown,p:nth-child(5){color:gold}\" onload=\"handleLinkLoadEvent(this)\" onerror=\"handleLinkErrorEvent(this)\">\r\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"data:*/*,p:nth-child(6){color:orange}\" onload=\"handleLinkLoadEvent(this)\" onerror=\"handleLinkErrorEvent(this)\">\r\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/guest271314/451634131a32d6f302744f2cbee92512/raw/296db2d197f81f073eb1285f630ebcc87a53692c/crossOriginCSSRequestedWithLinkElement.css\" onload=\"handleLinkLoadEvent(this)\" onerror=\"handleLinkErrorEvent(this)\">\r\n\r\n</head>\r\n\r\n<body>\r\n  <p>.css</p>\r\n  <p>styleNoExtension</p>\r\n  <p>data URL without MIME type</p>\r\n  <p>data URL with \"unknown/unknown\" MIME type</p>\r\n  <p>data URL with \"application/unknown\" MIME type</p>\r\n  <p>data URL with \"*/*\" MIME type</p>\r\n  <p>crossOriginCSSRequestedWithLinkElement gist does not set Content-Type header</p>\r\n</body>\r\n\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\nplnkr https://plnkr.co/edit/wiEL5drnUvIGkdqmQQu2?p=preview.\r\n\r\nInteresting results: \r\n\r\n**Chromium 64**\r\n\r\nOnly dispatches `error` event for a requested gist https://gist.githubusercontent.com/guest271314/451634131a32d6f302744f2cbee92512/raw/296db2d197f81f073eb1285f630ebcc87a53692c/crossOriginCSSRequestedWithLinkElement.css where was attempting to satisfy \"cross-origin\" request test. MIME checking occurs for the cross-origin request as well\r\n\r\n```\r\nRefused to apply style from 'https://gist.githubusercontent.com/guest271314/451634131a32d6f302744f2cbee92512/raw/296db2d197f81f073eb1285f630ebcc87a53692c/crossOriginCSSRequestedWithLinkElement.css' because its MIME type ('text/plain') is not a supported stylesheet MIME type, and strict MIME checking is enabled.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `load` event is dispatched for the remaining requests.\r\n\r\nOnly the local request where `.css` extension is set has style applied to the element (the first `<p>` element).\r\n\r\n**Firefox 60**\r\n\r\nThe `load` event is dispatched for  the local request where `.css` extension is set has style applied to the element (the first `<p>` element); and for `data URL` with MIME type set to `\"*/*\"` (the sixth `<p>` element).\r\n\r\nThe error message for the cross-origin (gist) request\r\n\r\n```\r\nDOMException: The operation is insecure.\r\n https://gist.githubusercontent.com/guest271314/451634131a32d6f302744f2cbee92512/raw/296db2d197f81f073eb1285f630ebcc87a53692c/crossOriginCSSRequestedWithLinkElement.css\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `error` event is dispatched for the remainder of `<p>` elements.",
